    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0705" n="645" xml:id="pg645"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Dickinson.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 103.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 28, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>Inclosed herewith, I transmit you a copy of a dispatch<anchor n="*"
                        xml:id="d374-f1"/> recently received from Charles Francis Adams, esq., in
                    reference to the misunderstanding of the British government with that of
                    Nicaragua.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. B. Dickinson</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d374-f1" n="*" xml:id="d374-f1-content">
                <p>For inclosure see dispatch No. 1530 from Mr. Adams, vol. I, p. 151.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
